# Backend

Full guide: `@docs/standards/BACKEND.md` · Conventions: `@docs/standards/CONVENTIONS.md` · Playbook: `@docs/standards/ADDING_A_FEATURE.md` · Upgrades: `@docs/standards/UPGRADES.md`

## Layout

- Keep code under `server/internal/` — no new `pkg/` or layer-folders (`models/`, `controllers/`)
- Register routes in `main.go`; one `ServeHTTP` handler type per domain
- Path/method switch after `TrimPrefix`; wrap with `RequirePermission` (public only for health + login)

## Must follow

- Schema changes **only** via named migrations in `internal/db/migrate.go`
- Append migrations only; new columns use a default; seeds must not replace user catalogs — full live-production policy in `@docs/standards/UPGRADES.md` (gate: `mudita-production`)
- Errors: JSON `{"error":"…"}`; money `*_mmk`; JSON `snake_case`
- New capability → `Perm*` + role map in `internal/auth/roles.go`
- Audit money-moving / sensitive mutations; receipts HTML on the server
- Split large domains into same-package files (e.g. `pharmacy_bills.go`) around ~800–1000 lines — not a new framework
- `gofmt`; avoid `util`/`common` dumping grounds
- Prefer nearest domain template: OPD (simple bills), OT (workflows), Pharmacy (stock)

## Stack

Go stdlib `net/http` ServeMux + SQLite WAL. Do not add Gin/Echo/chi or an ORM without an explicit decision.
